# TierDecay (always-on Project Rule)

This repo runs under the TierDecay protocol. The full adapter lives in
`AGENTS.md` at the repo root — treat every rule in it as binding, in
particular:

- Phase discipline: RECON → PLAN → EXECUTE → VERIFY → DISTILL; announce the
  current phase and route BEFORE touching code (playbook PROBE outranks ledger
  PRIORS; otherwise score the 4-axis rubric — ≥7 or any axis maxed = T3).
- State integrity: `.tierdecay/` is written ONLY during DISTILL. Any acceptance
  failure while a playbook entry was referenced → QUARANTINE it immediately.
  Never apply a QUARANTINE entry. Playbook hard cap: 150 lines.
- Every task closes with one ledger row in `.tierdecay/ledger.md`
  (class signature: 2–4 hyphenated tokens, `verb-object-surface` — reuse
  existing signatures). Full protocol reference: `.tierdecay/PROTOCOL.md`.

This rule exists so the protocol stays in context on every request even if
`AGENTS.md` auto-loading is disabled or trimmed. It intentionally duplicates
no detail: `AGENTS.md` is the single source of truth.
